hyphal_network.py was built step by step with the following prompts:

1. create a new script in the anastomosis/ folder. Create a function based on
   a hyphal length density (rho_h) and root tip density (rho_t) where the
   geometry is realized in a unit cube in 3D, hyphal lengths are a straight
   lines, root tips are the apical tips of these straight lines. I.e. start
   with inserting the tips into the cube (uniformly distributed) to achieve
   root tip density; in the next step add straight lines with a random angle
   (maximal length is towards the cube boundary) if more length is needed,
   add random hyphaes crossing the unit cube (i.e. having no root tip within
   the cube)

2. For an existing network (from create_hyphal_network) create a function
   that finds the number of hyphal tips that are next to other hyphae within
   a radius R. Store the hyphal network in a way, that it can be evaluated
   quickly for multiple radii R (i.e. to quickly find the minimal distance
   between hyphal tip and other hyphae)

3. add a plot with R that ranges from 0 to 0.2 for three different hyphal
   length densities (3 curves, different color, add legend)

4. can you do the same plot with 50 repitions (per curve) and plot mean and
   std, R from 0 to 0.3

5. can you do an additional plot, with 3 different tip densities for 160
   hyphal length (otherwise same as before)
